<title>BELGIUM: EU inflation at record low 2.3 pct in August.</title>
<headline>EU inflation at record low 2.3 pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inflation in the European Union reached a new record low in August, rising at an annualised rate of 2.3 percent, Eurostat, the EU's statistical office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Nine out of the 15-nation bloc registered inflation rates below 2.0 percent, with Sweden showing the smallest price rise of 0.3 percent while Greece put in the worst performance with inflation advancing at rate of 8.5 percent.</p>
<p>Following are the August annualised inflation rates for each country.</p>
<p>    Sweden	 0.3 pct	     Netherlands	1.9 pct</p>
<p>    Finland	0.4		   Britain	    2.1</p>
<p>    Luxembourg   1.4		   Denmark	    2.4</p>
<p>    Germany	1.4		   Italy		3.3</p>
<p>    Ireland	1.4		   Portugal	   3.6</p>
<p>    France	 1.6		   Spain		3.7</p>
<p>    Austria	1.8		   Greece	     8.5</p>
<p>    Belgium	1.9</p>
